cff-version: 1.2.0 message: “If you use this software in research,
please cite the specific version of the software used.” title:
“Reference-Neighbourhood Structural Context Framework” type: software
version: 0.1.0 authors: - family-names: “Harkess” given-names: “Michael”
license: Apache-2.0 abstract: >- An experimental computational framework
for representing and comparing materials through their relationship to a
reference materials population. The framework constructs a
Reference-Neighbourhood Fingerprint (RNF) for individual materials and
uses Candidate Context Analysis (CCA) to examine contextual similarity,
distinction, organisation, redundancy, clustering, and explainability
across candidate cohorts.
